A simple jenkins pipeline to verify if the docker slave configuration is working as expected.

pipeline {
  agent {
    docker { image 'node:16-alpine' }
  }
  stages {
    stage('Test') {
      steps {
        sh 'node --version'
      }
    }
  }
}

jenkins Master-slave node
---------------------------------
In old jenkins master slave approach there is a challenge that , if any ideal slave node , there is a resource utilised 
in background even if there is no job running on slave node. Also if I launch a slave node on cent-os 2.0 version , after
2 years there is upgrade verion will come , that devops person should upgrade. this way management issue also will face.

jenkins master as adocker agent 
---------------------------------------
where as latest approach jenkins as master with docker , if any job triggers then and there docker will create the container 
to run the required package for the build, once build completed container will stop and deleted. this is how we can save cost.
also need to maintain the slave node. 


Project -2  Multi Stage Multi Agent
==============

pipeline {
  agent none
  stages {
    stage('Back-end') {
      agent {
        docker { image 'maven:3.8.1-adoptopenjdk-11' }
      }
      steps {
        sh 'mvn --version'
      }
    }
    stage('Front-end') {
      agent {
        docker { image 'node:16-alpine' }
      }
      steps {
        sh 'node --version'
      }
    }
  }
}


